summary:
When I walk into a modern classroom now, I don’t just see audiovisual gear. I see endpoints.
The pan-tilt-zoom camera at the back of the room isn’t only for lecture capture now; it’s a sensor on the network. The speakers in the ceiling aren’t just to enhance video clips. On many campuses, they’re tied into an audio notification system that can push out warnings, lockdown messages or weather alerts.&nbsp;
The interactive flat panel or projector isn’t just a teaching surface. It’s a big, bright authenticated display that can just as easily show an emergency message as it can a presentation.…
